#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1051 expect=violation domain=SUPPDM
#note "Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner, queued item C3, as c5206c02): RDOMAIN names a domain, and dataset names match case-insensitively (owner 2026-10-01), so the literal comparison reads upper(RDOMAIN). Copy of PMDA-SD1051-invalid_idvar-SUPPDM.cdt with the RDOMAIN cells lower-cased; the expected outcome is the original one. Red under the old exact comparison."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 IDVAR=USUBJID
dataset SUPPDM label="Supplemental Qualifiers for DM"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | dm | 01-701-1015 |          |  | RACEOTH | ASIAN-INDIAN
CDISCPILOT01 | dm | 01-701-1023 | USUBJID  |  | RACEOTH | ASIAN-INDIAN
